    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69752" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάρκαφθον</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάσκαφθον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a fragrant Indianbark</i>, used
			as a spice, etc. (perh. the same as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάκαφθον</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.23
			</span></i>:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναόκαφθον</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάκαφθον</span></b>  in most codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				7.3
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάκαφθον</span></b>  in one
			cod. of <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.22.4
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάκαφθον</span>
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
